srow(159, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHEN YOU CROSS THE JORDAN" — WHY THIS SECTION? DEUTERONOMY 4:41 GAVE MOSES\' THREE ACROSS THE JORDAN; WHENCE THAT MOSES COMMANDED JOSHUA TO SET APART CITIES IN THE LAND? "YOU SHALL APPOINT CITIES" — AFTER INHERITANCE AND SETTLEMENT (DEUTERONOMY 19:1 "WHEN THE LORD CUTS OFF THE NATIONS"), NOT AT THE ENTRY; "TO THE LAND OF CANAAN" — R. YONATAN: THE JORDAN IS NOT OF CANAAN; R. SHIMON BEN YOCHAI: "BY THE JORDAN AT JERICHO" (36:13) — AS JERICHO IS, SO THE JORDAN; "CALLING OUT" IS DESIGNATION; "CITIES" — NOT WALLED TOWNS, NOT VILLAGES: MARKETS AND A FOOD STORE; "A SLAYER WHO SMITES A SOUL" — THE ONE WHO SMITES HIS FATHER AND MOTHER UNWITTINGLY IS NOT EXILED. The piska opens the shelf\'s return at 35:9 (the head asserted between 158 on 31:22 and 160 on 35:12). The row reads the crossing-clause as a timing clause by the parallel at {SP_(159, 1, "כי", "יכרית", "ה\'", "אלהיך")} ("when the LORD your God cuts off" — the Hebrew cites DEUTERONOMY 19, the refuge chapter\'s own opening 19:1, where the English cites 12:29: the clause stands at both, computed) — the settlement first, then the cities (I12, the context); the Jordan\'s status a DISPUTE on the phrase\'s two readings ({SP_(159, 1, "אין", "הירדן", "מארץ", "כנען")} "the Jordan is not of the land of Canaan" — the English cites 26:3 where the Hebrew names Numbers 36, the stamp\'s seven seats computed); "you shall appoint" read as designation — the ink\'s verb is the causative of "happen" (Balaam\'s meetings\' root, computed); the two "cities" tokens (35:11 "cities, cities of refuge" — the apposition\'s one seat) read as a size — {SP_(159, 1, "שווקים", "ובית", "המחיה")} ("markets and a house of provision"); and "a slayer who smites a soul" (the three-word phrase, five Bible seats) excluding the father-striker (Exodus 21:15 "he who smites his father and mother shall surely die" — the English supplies the citation the Hebrew lacks) from exile: the smiter of a parent is no "slayer". THE ENGLISH AND THE HEBREW: the citations differ at two seats, each read to its verse; the Hebrew has no "Shemot 21:15".')
srow(160, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"THE CITIES SHALL BE FOR YOU A REFUGE FROM THE AVENGER; THE SLAYER SHALL NOT DIE UNTIL HE STANDS BEFORE THE CONGREGATION FOR JUDGMENT" — WHY? BECAUSE 35:27 SAYS "THE AVENGER KILLS THE SLAYER, HE HAS NO BLOOD", I MIGHT THINK: BETWEEN THEMSELVES, AT ONCE; SCRIPTURE SAYS: NOT UNTIL THE COURT. The row reads 35:12 as the restriction on 35:27 — the avenger\'s license runs only after the standing before the congregation ({SP_(160, 1, "שומע", "אני", "בינו", "לבין", "עצמו", "יהרגנו")} "I might hear: between him and himself he may kill him"); THE INK: "he has no blood" the burglar\'s clause (Exodus 22:1) at its second seat, and the shelf\'s Hebrew writes the slayer PLENE ({SP_(160, 1, "הרוצח")}) where the ink writes him defective at every Numbers seat (computed); the "until" of 35:12 is the preposition, the "witness" of 35:30 its homograph (the lemmas, computed). ONKELOS goes further than the row at 35:19 and 21 — "when he has been found guilty by the court" supplied.')
srow(160, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"SIX CITIES OF REFUGE SHALL THERE BE" — TOGETHER WITH THE FIRST THREE (35:14 "THREE BEYOND THE JORDAN AND THREE IN CANAAN"): BEZER, RAMOTH, GOLAN (DEUTERONOMY 4:43) AND KEDESH, SHECHEM, HEBRON (JOSHUA 20:7) — TWO AND A HALF TRIBES MATCHED TO NINE AND A HALF, "MOST SPILLERS OF BLOOD IN GILEAD"; "SHALL BE FOR YOU" — REFUGE FOR KILLINGS OUTSIDE THE LAND TOO; "FOR THE CHILDREN OF ISRAEL ... AND THE STRANGER" — THE STRANGER WHO KILLED AN ISRAELITE IS KILLED, THE ISRAELITE WHO KILLED HIM EXEMPT (THE HEBREW: "ALL THE MORE NOT EXILED"); "THESE SIX" — NO CITY GIVES REFUGE UNTIL ALL SIX ARE SET APART. The row on 35:13-15 whole: the six as three plus three (the parser [3, 3] at 35:14; 35:13\'s six; the Sifrei\'s "with the first" against "exclusive of the first"); the six names read from Deuteronomy and Joshua — THE HEBREW MISQUOTES JOSHUA 20:7 ({SP_(160, 2, "היא", "חברון", "בארץ", "כנען")} "that is Hebron IN THE LAND OF CANAAN" for the ink\'s "in the hill country of Judah", computed); the Gilead remark ({SP_(160, 2, "שרוב", "שופכי", "דמים")} "that most spillers of blood" — the English adds Hosea 6:8 as a proof text); the stranger\'s case a DISPUTE resolved by "for you" — the English drops the Hebrew\'s a-fortiori ({SP_(160, 2, "ק\"ו", "שלא", "יגלה")} "all the more he is not exiled", computed); the rule that refuge begins when the sixth is set apart (Makkot 9b the exam\'s). THE INK: "the stranger and the sojourner" Abraham\'s pair; Joshua 20:9 keeps the stranger, drops the sojourner (computed).')
srow(160, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"IF WITH AN INSTRUMENT OF IRON HE STRUCK HIM" — WHY? FROM THE STONE AND THE WOOD I KNOW ONLY THOSE; IRON? — BUT IT FOLLOWS A FORTIORI: IF STONE AND WOOD MAKE HIM LIABLE, IRON THE MORE! EXCEPT THAT WE DO NOT PUNISH BY INFERENCE — SO "IRON" IS WRITTEN; "STONE OF THE HAND" — MUST IRON FILL THE HAND? IT WAS REVEALED THAT IRON KILLS AT ANY SIZE, SO "HAND" IS NOT WRITTEN OF IT — EVEN A NEEDLE; LUMPS THROWN AT HIM — "HE IS A MURDERER" IN ANY EVENT; "A STONE OF THE HAND WHEREBY HE MAY DIE" — AGAINST THE QUARREL OF EXODUS 21:18 ("WITH A STONE OR A FIST"): LIABLE ONLY BY A THING THAT CAN KILL AND (DEUTERONOMY 19:11) ON A PLACE THAT CAN KILL; ROCKS AND PILLARS ROLLED ON HIM — "IN ANY EVENT". The row on 35:16-17: the iron verse\'s omissions read — THE INK agrees to the token: the iron verse has ten tokens, no "hand", no "whereby he may die" (computed); THE RULE ABOUT RULES — {SP_(160, 3, "שאין", "עונשים", "מן", "הדין")} ("that we do not punish by inference") — carried by the Hebrew and DROPPED by the English (the same drop at 157:6, sitting 11\'s finding; a second instance), the a-fortiori (I1) refused on a penalty; "even a needle" ({SP_(160, 3, "אפילו", "מחט")}); the Hebrew\'s mistyped "Exodus 11" for 21:18 (computed); the two conditions on the stone (the thing and the place, Deuteronomy 19:11 "and strike him mortally") — the exam\'s Sanhedrin 76b. ONKELOS supplies the size clause at 17 and 18 as the row requires.')
srow(160, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"OR WITH A WOODEN INSTRUMENT OF THE HAND WHEREBY HE MAY DIE" — WHY? FROM EXODUS 21:20 (THE SLAVE STRUCK WITH A ROD) I MIGHT THINK ANY ROD; SCRIPTURE: ONLY A THING THAT CAN KILL, AND (DEUTERONOMY 19:11) ON A PLACE THAT CAN KILL; BEAMS AND POLES THROWN — "HE IS A MURDERER" IN ANY EVENT. The row on 35:18, the wood\'s twin of the stone\'s row: the slave-striker\'s rod (Exodus 21:20 "with a rod ... he shall surely be avenged" — the O7 head\'s span) as the case that needed the size clause ({SP_(160, 4, "בין", "שיש", "בו", "כדי", "להמיתו")} "whether there is in it enough to kill"); THE INK: "whereby he may die" with the masculine pronoun at 35:18 and at Elisha\'s sickness (2 Kings 13:14) alone (computed). Both files agree; the English\'s "hand-implement" its own compound.')
srow(160, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'THE ENGLISH ROW: "THE AVENGER, HE SHALL KILL THE MURDERER" — THE COMMANDMENT IS THE AVENGER\'S; ONE WHO HAS NO AVENGER — THE COURT APPOINTS ONE FOR HIM ("WHEN HE MEETS HIM", IN ANY EVENT). THE HEBREW ROW: "THE AVENGER OF BLOOD SHALL PUT THE MURDERER TO DEATH" — WHY? FROM THE STONE AND THE WOOD I KNOW ONLY THOSE; ANYTHING ELSE? BUILD THE PRINCIPLE FROM THE THREE: STONE IS NOT LIKE WOOD, WOOD NOT LIKE STONE, NEITHER LIKE IRON, IRON NOT LIKE THE TWO — THE COMMON FEATURE: IT CAN KILL, AND IF HE KILLED, THE COMMANDMENT IS IN THE AVENGER\'S HAND — SO ANYTHING THAT CAN KILL. THE TWO FILES CARRY DIFFERENT ROWS AT THIS ADDRESS (computed on the bytes): the Hebrew 160:5 is THE INDUCTION FROM THREE VERSES ({SP_(160, 5, "הרי", "אתה", "דן", "בנין", "אב", "מבין", "שלשתם")} "behold you reason a building-block from among the three" — the general principle built from several verses, I3\'s form with three fathers) ending {SP_(160, 5, "מצוה", "ביד", "גואל", "הדם")} ("the commandment is in the hand of the avenger of blood"); the English 160:5 is two sentences on the court-appointed avenger — the Hebrew\'s 160:7 tail, which the English 160:7 carries too — and the English 160:6 carries the induction instead: the rows TRANSPOSED between the files (RESEARCH_LOG.md). THE INK: "the avenger of blood, HE shall put to death" (35:19) — the pronoun the row reads as the commandment\'s assignment; the exam\'s Sanhedrin 45b on the court\'s appointed avenger.')
srow(160, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"IF IN HATRED HE THRUST HIM" — WHY? FROM THE IRON, THE STONE AND THE WOOD I KNOW ONLY THOSE; PUSHED HIM FROM A ROOF AND HE FELL AND DIED? "IN HATRED HE THRUST HIM" — IN ANY EVENT; BUT PUSHED HIM INTO WATER OR FIRE, OR SET A DOG OR A SNAKE ON HIM? BUILD THE PRINCIPLE FROM THE THREE — THE COMMON FEATURE: THEY KILL BY THE KILLING THINGS THEMSELVES — TO EXCLUDE THE WATER, THE FIRE AND THE SNAKE, WHOSE JUDGMENT IS GIVEN TO HEAVEN; "THREW AT HIM IN LYING-IN-WAIT" — HE HUNTED HIM, INTENDING HIM. The row on 35:20: the thrust without an instrument included by the verse ({SP_(160, 6, "דחפו", "מראש", "הגג")} "pushed him from the top of the roof"), the indirect killings excluded by the induction from the three (I3 with three fathers again — the English\'s 160:6 carries the Hebrew 160:5\'s induction before this one) — {SP_(160, 6, "שדינו", "מסור", "לשמים")} ("whose judgment is handed to Heaven"): THE HEAVEN ENTRY, the ledger\'s class for a debt no court collects (the effects law\'s vocabulary); "lying-in-wait" read as intent ({SP_(160, 6, "שצודה", "לו", "שמתכוון", "לו")} "that he hunts him, that he intends him") — THE INK: the noun\'s two Bible seats both this chapter\'s, its verb Exodus 21:13\'s spec (computed). The exam\'s Sanhedrin 77a-b (the water, the fire, the snake).')
srow(160, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"OR IN ENMITY HE STRUCK HIM WITH HIS HAND" — WHY? FROM THE THREE INSTRUMENTS I KNOW ONLY THOSE; CRUSHED HIM, STRANGLED HIM, KICKED HIM, TRAMPLED HIM? "WITH HIS HAND" — IN ANY MANNER; "THE AVENGER OF BLOOD SHALL PUT THE MURDERER TO DEATH" — IS IT NOT ALREADY SAID (35:19)? ONE WHO HAS NO AVENGER — "THE AVENGER OF BLOOD", IN ANY EVENT. The row on 35:21: the hand\'s four manners ({SP_(160, 7, "דחפו", "חנקו", "בעטו", "דעכו")} "pushed him, strangled him, kicked him, trampled him"); the doubled avenger-clause (35:19 and 35:21, the ink\'s two "when he meets him") read for the avengerless victim — {SP_(160, 7, "מי", "שאין", "לו", "גואל", "מנין")} ("one who has no avenger — whence?"), the clause both files carry here and the English carries again at its 160:5. THE INK: "the smiter" the participle (the quarrel\'s striker\'s word, Exodus 21:19), the enmity-noun the serpent\'s (Genesis 3:15) (computed).')
srow(160, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'"IF SUDDENLY, WITHOUT ENMITY" — TO EXCLUDE THE UNWITTING; "ANY INSTRUMENT WITHOUT LYING-IN-WAIT" — NOT HUNTING HIM, NOT INTENDING HIM; "ANY STONE WHEREBY HE MAY DIE, WITHOUT SEEING" — TO INCLUDE THE BLIND MAN AND THE NIGHT-THROWER; R. YEHUDAH: TO EXCLUDE THE BLIND; "HE WAS NOT HIS ENEMY" — ISSI BEN AKIVA: HIS STRINGENCY IS HIS LENIENCY — NEITHER DEATH (PERHAPS UNWITTING) NOR EXILE (PERHAPS WILFUL) CAN BE IMPOSED; "NOT HIS ENEMY" WITH "THE CONGREGATION SHALL JUDGE" — HATERS DISQUALIFIED FROM JUDGING; KIN — FROM "BETWEEN THE SMITER AND THE AVENGER"; WITNESSES — BY THE LIKENESS OF JUDGES AND WITNESSES, AND A FORTIORI (WITNESSES DECIDE THE FACTS); ALL CAPITAL CASES — "BY THESE JUDGMENTS"; THE STRANGER — LEVITICUS 24:22 "ONE JUDGMENT"; MONETARY CASES — NOT BY TWENTY-THREE (EXODUS 22:8); CAPITAL CASES BY TWENTY-THREE: "THE CONGREGATION SHALL JUDGE", "THE CONGREGATION SHALL DELIVER" — TEN AND TEN; THREE MORE: "DO NOT FOLLOW THE MANY FOR EVIL" (EXODUS 23:2) — THE INCLINING JUDGES AS THE WITNESSES ARE TWO, AND A COURT IS NOT EVEN: ADD ONE. The chapter\'s longest row, on 35:22-24: the unwitting cases\' clauses read one by one, the blind man a DISPUTE ({SP_(160, 8, "להביא", "את", "הסומא")} "to include the blind man" against R. Yehudah\'s exclusion), Issi ben Akiva\'s two-way uncertainty ({SP_(160, 8, "חומרו", "קולו", "וקולו", "חומרו")} "his stringency is his leniency and his leniency his stringency") — the row\'s TEIKU-shaped case: neither penalty; the disqualification of haters and kin from the bench by the juxtaposition (I12) and carried to witnesses by the likeness of the two "kill by" clauses and an a-fortiori (I1: judges do not decide the facts, witnesses do); the court\'s number built from the two congregation-tokens of 35:24-25 (ten and ten — the ink\'s "congregation" at 24, 25, 25, and 12; computed) plus three from Exodus 23:2\'s inclining ({SP_(160, 8, "ואין", "בית", "דין", "שקול")} "and a court is not evenly balanced") — TWENTY-THREE in the Hebrew ({SP_(160, 8, "בעשרים", "ושלשה")}), "THIRTY" IN THE ENGLISH, with the English\'s "[27]" for the tokens\' seats and the Mishnah\'s acquittal-by-one / conviction-by-two SUPPLIED where the Hebrew has "as witnesses are two, so judges" (computed on the bytes; RESEARCH_LOG.md); the closing remark on the three "congregations" of the section is the {SP_(160, 8, "דורשי", "רשומות")} ("expounders of the marked words"). The exam\'s Sanhedrin 2a-b and 27b (the kin), the seat of the court of twenty-three.')
srow(160, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'"THE CONGREGATION SHALL DELIVER ... AND RETURN HIM" — ALL WHO KILL, UNWITTING OR WILFUL, GO FIRST TO THE CITIES OF REFUGE; THE COURT SENDS AND BRINGS THEM: THE ONE LIABLE TO DEATH IS KILLED, THE ONE NOT LIABLE IS RELEASED, THE ONE LIABLE TO EXILE IS RETURNED TO HIS PLACE; "UNTIL THE DEATH OF THE HIGH PRIEST" — R. MEIR: THE MURDERER SHORTENS A MAN\'S DAYS, THE HIGH PRIEST LENGTHENS THEM; REBBI: THE MURDERER DEFILES THE LAND AND REMOVES THE PRESENCE, THE HIGH PRIEST BRINGS THE PRESENCE TO REST ON THE LAND — THE ONE SHOULD NOT STAND BEFORE THE OTHER. The row on 35:25: the procedure — {SP_(160, 9, "הכל", "מקדימים", "לערי", "מקלט")} ("all go first to the cities of refuge"), the court\'s three verdicts; the term explained two ways (a DISPUTE of reasons, no rule moved) — R. Meir\'s days ({SP_(160, 9, "רוצח", "מקצר", "ימיו", "של", "אדם")} "a murderer shortens a man\'s days") and Rebbi\'s Presence, the Presence-reason 35:34\'s own clause read back onto 35:25 (I12). THE INK: the high priest DEFECTIVE here alone; the anointing clause one seat (computed); the exam\'s Makkot 11a-b on the three high priests and the death that releases.')
srow(160, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'"IF THE SLAYER GOING OUT GOES OUT" — R. ELAZAR BEN AZARIAH: IF UNDER THE LESSER MEASURE, PUNISHMENT, ONE STEP OUT FORFEITS THE SOUL, HOW MUCH MORE UNDER THE GREATER MEASURE, REWARD; "THE AVENGER FINDS HIM" — ANY MAN; "FOR IN HIS CITY OF REFUGE HE SHALL DWELL" — ONE WHO KILLED IN THAT CITY IS EXILED FROM QUARTER TO QUARTER, A LEVITE FROM CITY TO CITY; "AFTER THE DEATH OF THE HIGH PRIEST THE SLAYER RETURNS" — NOT TO HIS OFFICE (R. YEHUDAH); EVEN TO HIS OFFICE (R. MEIR). The row on 35:26-28: the doubled infinitive read by an a-fortiori from the measures ({SP_(160, 10, "מדת", "פורענות", "מועטת")} "the measure of punishment is small" — I1 across the two measures, the aggadic form of the rule "the measure of good exceeds"); "the avenger" widened to any man ({SP_(160, 10, "בכל", "אדם")}); the fugitive who kills inside the city ({SP_(160, 10, "גולה", "משכונה", "לשכונה")} "exiled from quarter to quarter") and the Levite\'s case; the returner\'s office a DISPUTE (R. Yehudah / R. Meir — the exam\'s Makkot 13a). THE ENGLISH marks the verses "(37)" and "(38)" for 27 and 28 (computed); the Hebrew\'s "going out" plene ({SP_(160, 10, "יצוא", "יצא")}) against the ink\'s defective first token (computed).')
srow(161, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"A STATUTE OF JUDGMENT FOR YOUR GENERATIONS" — FOR THE GENERATIONS; "IN ALL YOUR DWELLINGS" — IN THE LAND AND OUTSIDE IT; "WHOEVER SMITES A SOUL, BY WITNESSES SHALL HE SLAY" — WHY? FROM "THE AVENGER SHALL PUT HIM TO DEATH" I MIGHT THINK: BETWEEN THEMSELVES — R. YOSHIYAH: ONLY BY WITNESSES; R. YONATAN: IN COURT WITHOUT WITNESSES? — ONLY IN COURT AND BY WITNESSES; "ONE WITNESS SHALL NOT TESTIFY TO DEATH" — HE TESTIFIES FOR ACQUITTAL; ONE WITNESS OBLIGES AN OATH; AND THE PROTOTYPE: WHEREVER "WITNESS" IS WRITTEN, TWO ARE MEANT, UNLESS SCRIPTURE SPECIFIES "ONE"; "YOU SHALL NOT TAKE RANSOM FOR THE LIFE OF A MURDERER" — WHY? EXODUS 21:30 RANSOMS THE OX\'S OWNER, DEATH AT HEAVEN\'S HAND; DEATH BY MAN? — "YOU SHALL NOT TAKE"; R. YOSHIYAH: ONE GOING OUT TO EXECUTION WHO INJURED OTHERS IS LIABLE; OTHERS WHO INJURED HIM — EXEMPT FOR HIS BODY, LIABLE FOR HIS PROPERTY; "WHO IS WICKED TO DIE" — BEFORE THE VERDICT IS FINISHED, LIABLE; AFTER, EXEMPT; R. YONATAN: ONE WHO KILLED HIM ON THE WAY — EXEMPT AFTER THE VERDICT. The piska opens the chapter\'s law-statute (the Hebrew carries this row twice — 160:11 and here, the duplicate dropping a letter: {SP_(160, 11, "ל", "מכה", "נפש")} for {SP_(161, 1, "כל", "מכה", "נפש")}, computed); "in all your dwellings" read as the court\'s reach outside the land ({SP_(161, 1, "בארץ", "ובח\"ל")} "in the land and outside the land" — the Sabbath\'s and the blood\'s formula, Leviticus 3:17, at its second seat, computed); the two readings of 35:30\'s first clause a DISPUTE of what the verse adds to 35:19; THE PROTOTYPE — {SP_(161, 1, "זה", "בנה", "אב")} ("this builds a father", I3): "witness" means two unless "one" is written — the ink\'s bare plural "witnesses" at 35:30 (one seat) against Deuteronomy\'s numbered pairs (computed); THE RANSOM against the goring ox (Exodus 21:30, the ox\'s ransom for a death at Heaven\'s hand — the exam\'s Bava Kamma 40a; the half-shekel\'s "ransom for his soul" the noun\'s other Torah seat, computed) — THE ENGLISH INSERTS "Whence is this derived? From \'And you shall not take ransom\'" where the Hebrew has no derivation (computed); the condemned man\'s liabilities before and after the verdict (the exam\'s Sanhedrin 71b, Arakhin 6b).')
srow(161, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU SHALL NOT TAKE RANSOM FOR ONE WHO FLED TO HIS CITY OF REFUGE" — ONE WHO KILLED WILFULLY: I MIGHT THINK HE MAY PAY AND BE EXILED INSTEAD; SCRIPTURE: NO RANSOM TO FLEE THERE. The row on 35:32 (the Hebrew\'s 160:12 the duplicate): the second refusal read for the wilful killer buying exile ({SP_(161, 2, "אם", "יתן", "ממון", "ויגלה")} "if he gives money and is exiled?") — the Sifrei\'s reading, against the plain sense of the unwitting fugitive buying his return; ONKELOS "money" for the ransom at both seats (computed). THE INK: "until the death of the priest" without "great" at this one seat (computed); the exam\'s Ketubot 37b.')
srow(161, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU SHALL NOT POLLUTE THE LAND" — AN EXHORTATION AGAINST THE FLATTERERS; OR: DO NOT CAUSE THE LAND TO FLATTER YOU; "FOR THE BLOOD, IT POLLUTES" — R. YOSHIYAH\'S NOTARIKON: "IT RESTS WRATH ON THE LAND"; "AND FOR THE LAND NO ATONEMENT" — WHY? DEUTERONOMY 21:4 BREAKS THE HEIFER\'S NECK; IF ITS NECK WAS BROKEN AND THEN THE SLAYER FOUND, I MIGHT THINK ATONEMENT WAS MADE — NO ATONEMENT FOR THE LAND; "YOU SHALL NOT DEFILE THE LAND" — BLOODSHED DEFILES THE LAND AND REMOVES THE PRESENCE, AND FOR BLOODSHED THE TEMPLE WAS DESTROYED. The row on 35:33-34 (the Hebrew\'s 160:13 the duplicate): the pollute-verb\'s two senses — the flatterer\'s (the root\'s adjective at Isaiah, Job, Proverbs — the token family computed) and the land\'s fruit withheld ({SP_(161, 3, "שתהא", "מחנפת", "לכם")} "that it be flattering you"); THE NOTARIKON — {SP_(161, 3, "כי", "הדם", "יחון", "אף", "בארץ")} ("for the blood will rest wrath on the land"): the verb split into two words (E30, the word-split; MIDDOT.md\'s case law), R. Yoshiyah\'s; THE HEIFER\'S CASE — Deuteronomy 21:4 cited, the unknown slayer found after the rite ({SP_(161, 3, "ואחר", "כך", "נמצא", "ההורג")} "and afterwards the killer was found") — the land\'s rule wins: no atonement but the shedder\'s blood (the Mishnah Sotah 9:7 the exam\'s); THE INK: the pollute-root\'s only Torah seat, Psalm 106:38\'s echo with the blood, the ransom\'s root as the atonement\'s (computed). Both files agree; the English adds no citation for the heifer\'s verse beyond the Hebrew\'s "Deuteronomy 21".')
srow(161, 4, 'CONTEXT', f'IT HAPPENED THAT TWO PRIESTS, EQUAL, RAN UP THE RAMP; ONE OUTRAN THE OTHER WITHIN FOUR CUBITS, TOOK A KNIFE AND DROVE IT INTO HIS HEART; R. TZADOK STOOD ON THE STEPS OF THE HALL: "HEAR ME, OUR BROTHERS THE HOUSE OF ISRAEL — \'IF A SLAIN MAN BE FOUND IN THE LAND\' (DEUTERONOMY 21:1): COME, LET US MEASURE FOR WHOM THE HEIFER IS DUE — THE HALL OR THE COURT"; ALL ISRAEL WEPT; THE BOY\'S FATHER CAME: "MY BROTHERS, I AM YOUR ATONEMENT — MY SON STILL WRITHES AND THE KNIFE IS NOT DEFILED" — THE CLEANNESS OF KNIVES DEARER TO THEM THAN BLOODSHED; SO 2 KINGS 21:16, MANASSEH FILLING JERUSALEM WITH INNOCENT BLOOD FROM END TO END: FOR BLOODSHED THE PRESENCE DEPARTS AND THE SANCTUARY IS DEFILED. A story-row, the Temple\'s own instance of 35:33\'s land-rule (the Hebrew\'s 160:14 the duplicate; the Tosefta and the Talmud\'s Yoma 23a the exam\'s seat); the heifer\'s measuring ({SP_(161, 4, "בואו", "ונמדוד")} "come and let us measure" — the measure-verb of Deuteronomy 21:2, the verb of 35:5\'s pasture-lands, computed) turned on the Temple itself; the row\'s citations — the English "Devarim 21:1" for the Hebrew\'s bare "Deuteronomy 21", the Kings verse in parentheses here and bare at the duplicate (computed on the bytes). CONTEXT: an incident, not a rule.')
srow(161, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"IN WHOSE MIDST I DWELL" — BELOVED ARE ISRAEL: EVEN WHEN UNCLEAN THE PRESENCE IS AMONG THEM (LEVITICUS 16:16 "WHO DWELLS WITH THEM IN THE MIDST OF THEIR UNCLEANNESS", 15:31, NUMBERS 5:3 "THEIR CAMP IN WHOSE MIDST I DWELL", 35:34); R. NATAN: WHEREVER THEY WERE EXILED THE PRESENCE WAS WITH THEM — EGYPT (1 SAMUEL 2:27), BABYLON (ISAIAH 43:14), ELAM (JEREMIAH 49:38), EDOM (ISAIAH 63:1) — AND WHEN THEY RETURN IT RETURNS WITH THEM: "THE LORD WILL RETURN WITH YOUR CAPTIVITY" (DEUTERONOMY 30:3) — NOT "BRING BACK" BUT "RETURN"; "WITH ME FROM LEBANON, BRIDE" (SONG 4:8); REBBI: A KING TO HIS SERVANTS — IF YOU SEEK ME, I AM WITH MY SON. The book\'s last row (the Hebrew closing with the colophon {SP_(161, 5, "סליק", "להו", "ספר", "במדבר", "סיני")} "the book of Numbers is completed" — the English drops it, computed): 35:34\'s "in whose midst I dwell" read with its inclusio-twin 5:3 (the Sifrei 1:7, credited, read the same pair from the other end — THE INK: the two seats of "I dwell in the midst" in the Torah, the book\'s first law and its last, computed) and Leviticus 16:16\'s "who dwells with them in their uncleanness"; R. Natan\'s four exiles by four proof texts (each read to its verse — 1 Samuel 2:27 "did I not reveal myself to your father\'s house in Egypt"; the Babylon, Elam and Edom verses; computed); THE STEM READ — {SP_(161, 5, "והשיב", "לא", "נאמר", "אלא", "ושב")} ("\'and he will bring back\' is not said, but \'and he will return\'"): Deuteronomy 30:3\'s simple stem read against the causative (the ink\'s form the simple, computed) — the Presence returns as one of the captives (the exam\'s Megillah 29a); Rebbi\'s parable. The Hebrew\'s nine parentheses include Song of Songs and "Numbers 35" (computed).')
